The current estimator’s main strength is moment-matched Monte Carlo: it forces the sampled input covariance to match the true Gaussian before the first layer. I’m going to compare that against one-block sampling, smaller fractions, and a cheap analytic blend on generated MLPs before risking blackbox time.
